# Go binaries and build artifacts
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Test binary built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Coverage output
*.out
coverage.out

# Vendor directory (we don't vendor) — except internal/web/assets/vendor/,
# which holds the PLAN-5 / C8 HTMX bundle committed verbatim so
# `go install` produces a self-contained binary with no toolchain.
vendor/
/vendor/
!internal/web/assets/vendor/
!internal/web/assets/vendor/**

# goreleaser output
/dist/

# Local binary output (e.g., from `make build`)
/ape
/aped
/bin/

# Editor / IDE
.vscode/
.VSCodeCounter

# Local logs / scratch
/logs/
*/logs/
*/*/logs/
*.db

# Temporary local override

# /output/ — matches only a directory named output at the repository root
#  (e.g., output/), not in subdirectories
# The leading / anchors the pattern to the root of the repo.
/output/

# Advisory-lock sidecar left by `ape sprint reconcile`. It is a runtime
# artifact — the lock is released, but the file is deliberately not unlinked
# (deleting a lock another process may hold loses the mutual exclusion).
# The same entry `ape framework setup` writes into a project, and narrower
# than `*.lock` on purpose: Cargo.lock and friends belong in history.
sprint-status.yaml.lock

# The shared board's state (`ape aboard`). Gitignored on purpose: a board is a
# LOCAL, persistent, non-authoritative channel — several developers on one repo
# each get their own, and a committed one is a whole-file JSON conflict on every
# merge over a conversation that was never theirs. Conclusions reached on a board
# get promoted into committed artifacts; the board itself never is.
.aboard/

# Run artifacts ape writes INTO a test fixture when a command is pointed at
# one. `resolveMonotonic` issues a timestamp for every project-data command,
# and its persisted floor lands under the fixture's own output folder — so
# merely running `ape sprint check --cwd testdata/apexproject` leaves a file
# behind. One was committed once; this is why it cannot happen twice.
#
# Scoped to testdata rather than a bare `_output/`: a project's output folder
# is framework-owned and named by config, and a blanket rule here would be a
# claim about other people's repositories.
testdata/*/_output/
